# Secrets — never commit. scripts/setup-git.sh refuses to run without this line.
.env

# Generated output. The deploy swaps site/ by rename, so a release leaves a
# site-backup-* copy behind (and a site-failed-* one if a live check fails);
# staging-* is the build target before the swap. daily.py commits explicit
# paths and would never add them, but `git add -A`, which we use by hand,
# would sweep a whole copy of the site into the public repository.
site/
site-preview/
_replay/
site-backup-*/
site-failed-*/
staging-*/

# Data cache. Re-downloaded by data.refresh() on every run, and the current
# season's file changes constantly — committing it would show the tree as
# permanently modified and bury the ledger commits, which are the evidence,
# under a stream of noise.
data/

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# The OpenTimestamps client caches calendar responses in $HOME/.cache,
# and this service's home IS the repository root. daily.py commits explicit
# paths so the job would never add it — but `git add -A`, which we use by
# hand, would sweep it straight into the public ledger repository.
.cache/

# Vendored club crests. scripts/vendor_crests.py downloads them from the
# providers into static/clubs/ so the site serves its own images instead of
# hotlinking a third-party CDN through a launch. They are protected marks
# belonging to the clubs: serving them on the site is one thing, shipping 216
# of them inside a public repository is a broader redistribution than this
# project has any right to, and the repo's job is to carry the evidence, not
# the decoration. A deliberately licensed asset pack would be committed here
# instead, under the same names.
static/clubs/

# Session backups (rollback artefacts, not record)
*.bak*

# Operational noise from OnFailure=, not record.
failures.log

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp

# SSH deploy key - never commit.
.ssh/
